(2401310, 328970, 40343, '<td valign="top">lol I knew this wouldn''t sdo that well , but to do SO badly makes me laugh!<br/> <br/>thanks Dr Timbo , arnit and eveyone with positive comments<br/> <br/>just to clarify<br/> <br/>THIS IS A DELIBERATE SHOT. no need for a tripod, no camera shake etc...<br/> <br/>to re-create the you need a funky shadow, soft as possible (i had to deliberatly lower the light)<br/>the image you get doesn''t really look like anything UNTIL the post-shot work (in my case in photoshop)<br/>and then its a case of getting the different tones out, the fullsize image has an amazing grain and texture to it, I''ll post it online somewhere<br/> <br/>and thanks regarding the cinematic look as that''s totally what i was going for that and slightly creepy - after all it''s a grim, fairy tale<br/> <br/>what i didn''t want to produce was a beautiful sunset with a path through a forest of lush leaves! :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-10 12:22:39.</i></td>', 'lol I knew this wouldn''t sdo that well , but to do SO badly makes me laugh! thanks Dr Timbo , arnit and eveyone with positive comments just to clarify THIS IS A DELIBERATE SHOT. no need for a tripod, no camera shake etc... to re-create the you need a funky shadow, soft as possible (i had to deliberatly lower the light)the image you get doesn''t really look like anything UNTIL the post-shot work (in my case in photoshop)and then its a case of getting the different tones out, the fullsize image has an amazing grain and texture to it, I''ll post it online somewhere and thanks regarding the cinematic look as that''s totally what i was going for that and slightly creepy - after all it''s a grim, fairy tale what i didn''t want to produce was a beautiful sunset with a path through a forest of lush leaves! :-)', '2006-05-10 13:19:07.000000', '2006-05-10 13:22:39.000000', 0),
(2401312, 327458, 49652, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the Blue!  Stunning picture.</td>', 'Congrats on the Blue!  Stunning picture.', '2006-05-10 13:19:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401318, 328970, 40343, '<td valign="top"><a href="//flickr.com/photo_zoom.gne?id=138974384&amp;context=set-72057594128859090&amp;size=l" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">link to larger image on flickr</a></td>', 'link to larger image on flickr', '2006-05-10 13:20:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401428, 327796, 40718, '<td valign="top">A few thoughts:<br/> <br/>1) The subject is tough.  In reality it''s excellent and of course you think this dog is the most beautiful thing in the world where others might see an old decrepid dog.  Perfect application of the saying, BUT in our weird world, people still want to see pictures of appealing things.  You probably lost a bit for having the guts to take a picture which may not have mass appeal. (That''s not a bad thing! It just doesn''t help your score.)<br/> <br/>2) The focus does seem just a bit soft.  I''m not sure if it is DOF, OOF, or motion blur (even though you were at 1/250th).  You can see this most apparent in the fur at the top of his head.<br/> <br/>3) Perhaps to compensate for the focus, it seems a bit oversharp.  If not, it may be just a bit too contrasty (which I rarely say in 4.7-5.3 pictures).<br/> <br/>4) The square crop isn''t the best.  I would have actually made it more vertical so you had some negative space to move the dog slightly off center.<br/> <br/>5) The conversion to B&amp;W is pretty good.  I think you did a good job there.</td>', 'A few thoughts: 1) The subject is tough.  In reality it''s excellent and of course you think this dog is the most beautiful thing in the world where others might see an old decrepid dog.  Perfect application of the saying, BUT in our weird world, people still want to see pictures of appealing things.  You probably lost a bit for having the guts to take a picture which may not have mass appeal. (That''s not a bad thing! It just doesn''t help your score.) 2) The focus does seem just a bit soft.  I''m not sure if it is DOF, OOF, or motion blur (even though you were at 1/250th).  You can see this most apparent in the fur at the top of his head. 3) Perhaps to compensate for the focus, it seems a bit oversharp.  If not, it may be just a bit too contrasty (which I rarely say in 4.7-5.3 pictures). 4) The square crop isn''t the best.  I would have actually made it more vertical so you had some negative space to move the dog slightly off center. 5) The conversion to B&W is pretty good.  I think you did a good job there.', '2006-05-10 13:43:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401437, 328823, 43434, '<td valign="top">Fantastic explainantion and fantastic story .. its great to see what else is behind a picture.</td>', 'Fantastic explainantion and fantastic story .. its great to see what else is behind a picture.', '2006-05-10 13:45:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401457, 327921, 40718, '<td valign="top">Well, when you start by saying yourself "this is a bad pic"... ;)<br/> <br/>I hadn''t seen which challenge this was an originally wondered if it was for rhythm with the repeated lines.  Being cliche, I think the perspective angle you took is too severe.  The A/C unit, or whatever that thing is, is distracting and the tagging isn''t even that pretty. (apparently you need some more talented vandals around your area.)<br/> <br/>I''m guessing you knew this would score like this going in.  I call that dead pixels walking.  No amount of PP is going to save a picture that is uninspired to begin with.  You made an attempt with the boosted contrast trying to give a edgy urban feel, but it wasn''t up to the task.  With this picture in mind, I suggest working more on subject choice.  Look for something that grabs the eye in its unusualness, shape, texture, etc....</td>', 'Well, when you start by saying yourself "this is a bad pic"... ;) I hadn''t seen which challenge this was an originally wondered if it was for rhythm with the repeated lines.  Being cliche, I think the perspective angle you took is too severe.  The A/C unit, or whatever that thing is, is distracting and the tagging isn''t even that pretty. (apparently you need some more talented vandals around your area.) I''m guessing you knew this would score like this going in.  I call that dead pixels walking.  No amount of PP is going to save a picture that is uninspired to begin with.  You made an attempt with the boosted contrast trying to give a edgy urban feel, but it wasn''t up to the task.  With this picture in mind, I suggest working more on subject choice.  Look for something that grabs the eye in its unusualness, shape, texture, etc....', '2006-05-10 13:50:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401499, 328457, 4517, '<td valign="top">Haven`t you got any patients to treat or something :)</td>', 'Haven`t you got any patients to treat or something :)', '2006-05-10 13:58:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401533, 329201, 40374, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, well done. <br/></td>', 'Congratulations, well done. ', '2006-05-10 14:07:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401576, 327458, 45559, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your blue!</td>', 'Congrats on your blue!', '2006-05-10 14:15:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401674, 327988, 40718, '<td valign="top">Yes, baby pics do suffer some here, although they don''t always.  I gave this a 4 for pretty well one reason.  The lighting.  It looks very blue which never makes skin very pretty.<br/> <br/>Pull up your photo in PS and adjust the color balance to +30/0/-30 (meaning more red and yellow).  Now go back and forth to the before and after.  You can see how she seems to come to life more.<br/> <br/>If you used a flash on the picture it is the culprit for the color cast.  The camera had a tough time setting the WB because there are no true grays in the picture.<br/> <br/>Her shoulder is also blown out which makes the eye want to drift up there instead of her darling face.</td>', 'Yes, baby pics do suffer some here, although they don''t always.  I gave this a 4 for pretty well one reason.  The lighting.  It looks very blue which never makes skin very pretty. Pull up your photo in PS and adjust the color balance to +30/0/-30 (meaning more red and yellow).  Now go back and forth to the before and after.  You can see how she seems to come to life more. If you used a flash on the picture it is the culprit for the color cast.  The camera had a tough time setting the WB because there are no true grays in the picture. Her shoulder is also blown out which makes the eye want to drift up there instead of her darling face.', '2006-05-10 14:41:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401722, 328952, 57622, '<td valign="top">Thank you for your comments on my first submitted challenge. Each was very helpful. I did want a hi key effect for this image. The bird is named Charley. The gossip; you''ll have to talk to Charley.<br/> <br/>Karen</td>', 'Thank you for your comments on my first submitted challenge. Each was very helpful. I did want a hi key effect for this image. The bird is named Charley. The gossip; you''ll have to talk to Charley. Karen', '2006-05-10 14:52:04.000000', NULL, 0),
