(2403820, 329309, 42125, '<td valign="top">Comment from a member of your own commenting club :-)<br/><b>First impression</b> <br/>1. Good selection of a Cliché<br/>2. The stitch is irregular<br/>3. Good focus and contrast<br/>4. Cropping is good using rule of thirds.<br/><b>What could be better</b> <br/>1. I find the picture to dark and therefore added lighting would help.<br/>2. IMO the stich could have been better looking but this is just IMO.<br/>3. A frame to close the picture.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Comment from a member of your own commenting club :-)First impression 1. Good selection of a Cliché2. The stitch is irregular3. Good focus and contrast4. Cropping is good using rule of thirds.What could be better 1. I find the picture to dark and therefore added lighting would help.2. IMO the stich could have been better looking but this is just IMO.3. A frame to close the picture. ', '2006-05-10 21:52:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2403891, 328163, 42125, '<td valign="top">Comment from a member of your own commenting club :-) <br/><b>First impression</b> <br/>1. Mirror :-)<br/>2. Beautiful woman<br/>3. Good natural lighting<br/>4. Good focus and contrast on the yonger one<br/>5. Cropping is good, making rule of thirds in action.<br/>6. The colours are bright and alive!<br/>7. Good choice of a Cliché<br/><b>What could be better</b> <br/>1. Better focus on the older one<br/>2. As you say, the background is a bit distracting and divides the picture in two. Giving this mirror effect so I am not so sure if it a bad thing after all. <br/></td>', 'Comment from a member of your own commenting club :-) First impression 1. Mirror :-)2. Beautiful woman3. Good natural lighting4. Good focus and contrast on the yonger one5. Cropping is good, making rule of thirds in action.6. The colours are bright and alive!7. Good choice of a ClichéWhat could be better 1. Better focus on the older one2. As you say, the background is a bit distracting and divides the picture in two. Giving this mirror effect so I am not so sure if it a bad thing after all. ', '2006-05-10 22:11:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2403893, 327584, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/>Heh!  You seem to do really well with the humorous pictures!  Great shot to go with the caption/title.  Biggest problem is the fence top behind the bear which is blown and pulls the eye away from the bear.  A tighter crop keeping the log just beyond his foot "whole" would compensate a bit.  The expression you captured is priceless!</td>', 'Trading Post commentHeh!  You seem to do really well with the humorous pictures!  Great shot to go with the caption/title.  Biggest problem is the fence top behind the bear which is blown and pulls the eye away from the bear.  A tighter crop keeping the log just beyond his foot "whole" would compensate a bit.  The expression you captured is priceless!', '2006-05-10 22:12:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2403927, 328884, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/>I didn''t vote in this challenge, but when I scrolled through, this one made me laugh.  Great idea!  Need a bit more light to define the eyes and it would have been more effective with more blue.  :-)  Good job with the skin tones, and I like the crop!</td>', 'Trading Post commentI didn''t vote in this challenge, but when I scrolled through, this one made me laugh.  Great idea!  Need a bit more light to define the eyes and it would have been more effective with more blue.  :-)  Good job with the skin tones, and I like the crop!', '2006-05-10 22:20:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2403954, 329131, 20530, '<td valign="top">Oh, this was you? Loved it. I gave it an 8. I thought it was clever, creative and so interesting that I looked at it for quite a while. The reflection really made it pop. The little "hanging off pieces" bugged me a little. But, overall super cool shot!</td>', 'Oh, this was you? Loved it. I gave it an 8. I thought it was clever, creative and so interesting that I looked at it for quite a while. The reflection really made it pop. The little "hanging off pieces" bugged me a little. But, overall super cool shot!', '2006-05-10 22:27:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2403996, 328163, 38496, '<td valign="top">From... darn.. now I can''t remember the acronym... but the commenting club marquee II(as opposed to the Critique Club):<br/> <br/>I really like this picture.  Captures the cliche beautifully.  The ligthing is good, and the skin tones look spot on.  The only thing I don''t like so well is that the mother is slightly out of focus.  Then again maybe that was intentional, and could certainly work, making her look older and more ''washed out'', not as young and vibrant as the daughter?  I''m not sure I''d like that message though, given that I''m a mom Ü.<br/> <br/></td>', 'From... darn.. now I can''t remember the acronym... but the commenting club marquee II(as opposed to the Critique Club): I really like this picture.  Captures the cliche beautifully.  The ligthing is good, and the skin tones look spot on.  The only thing I don''t like so well is that the mother is slightly out of focus.  Then again maybe that was intentional, and could certainly work, making her look older and more ''washed out'', not as young and vibrant as the daughter?  I''m not sure I''d like that message though, given that I''m a mom Ü. ', '2006-05-10 22:40:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404045, 327995, 38496, '<td valign="top">from comment trading post:<br/> <br/>I like this idea a lot.  The names in the forground with the couple in the background works very well.<br/>The names on the boxes could be a little sharper, though.  It looks like maybe this is a tad too underexposed.  Adding a little more ligt would help.  That might help the overall color of the picture, too, which seems a little dark to me.  The color is also too yellow, with little contrast.  <br/>With some lighting correction this would be a really nice shot.</td>', 'from comment trading post: I like this idea a lot.  The names in the forground with the couple in the background works very well.The names on the boxes could be a little sharper, though.  It looks like maybe this is a tad too underexposed.  Adding a little more ligt would help.  That might help the overall color of the picture, too, which seems a little dark to me.  The color is also too yellow, with little contrast.  With some lighting correction this would be a really nice shot.', '2006-05-10 22:48:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404059, 327988, 41337, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2</b> <br/> <br/><b>First Impression:</b> <br/>Very cute.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I might have zoomed out a bit just so not to cut off the top part of her head but otherwise is good.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Works well for the challenge. <br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Not really much to add that DrAchoo hasn''t already covered. <br/> <br/><b>Improvement:</b> <br/>What DrAchoo said. Also, I would add maybe choosing a different cliche next time. Not because this didn''t fit the challenge but because you couldn''t show off her eyes. Eyes can be so powerful in a shot even when the rest of the image has a bunch of flaws so I''d keep that in mind in the future.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good photo overall. I don''t get those really low votes (1-3). That tells me there was a bias or they thought it didn''t meet the challenge, which I don''t get. Anyway, good luck in the future and I look forward to seeing more of your work. <br/></td>', 'Greetings from CTP2  First Impression: Very cute. Composition: I might have zoomed out a bit just so not to cut off the top part of her head but otherwise is good. Subject: Works well for the challenge.  Technical (Colour and light): Not really much to add that DrAchoo hasn''t already covered.  Improvement: What DrAchoo said. Also, I would add maybe choosing a different cliche next time. Not because this didn''t fit the challenge but because you couldn''t show off her eyes. Eyes can be so powerful in a shot even when the rest of the image has a bunch of flaws so I''d keep that in mind in the future. Summary: Good photo overall. I don''t get those really low votes (1-3). That tells me there was a bias or they thought it didn''t meet the challenge, which I don''t get. Anyway, good luck in the future and I look forward to seeing more of your work. ', '2006-05-10 22:52:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404073, 328884, 10818, '<td valign="top">Its a very good portrait.<br/> <br/>My first thought was, if you are going that far, why not go all the way, and do the whole face?  I would have left the chin in on the crop.<br/> <br/>Not bad at all though.  If I voted on the contest....6 or maybe 7.  but it had so much potential.</td>', 'Its a very good portrait. My first thought was, if you are going that far, why not go all the way, and do the whole face?  I would have left the chin in on the crop. Not bad at all though.  If I voted on the contest....6 or maybe 7.  but it had so much potential.', '2006-05-10 22:55:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404077, 328884, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post -<br/>Not quite sure about this one. I think you should have fully committed to the title and went all blue baby. I may have opted for a slightly tighter crop - taken the ears right out. Your lines on the nose are a little off which left the pic seeming a bit off balance. The lines on each side of your face seem symmetrical though. I think the lighting on your eyes was maybe in the middle of where it would have worked better. A little brighter to see the color and detail of your pupils or a littl edarker to make it more sinister.<br/> <br/>This shot did make me smile when I first saw it - but you would have scored much higher in my book had you just dipped your whole head in blue paint. That would have screamed dedication to your craft.</td>', 'Trading Post -Not quite sure about this one. I think you should have fully committed to the title and went all blue baby. I may have opted for a slightly tighter crop - taken the ears right out. Your lines on the nose are a little off which left the pic seeming a bit off balance. The lines on each side of your face seem symmetrical though. I think the lighting on your eyes was maybe in the middle of where it would have worked better. A little brighter to see the color and detail of your pupils or a littl edarker to make it more sinister. This shot did make me smile when I first saw it - but you would have scored much higher in my book had you just dipped your whole head in blue paint. That would have screamed dedication to your craft.', '2006-05-10 22:57:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404160, 328465, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique by <b><a href="//dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=332" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">arnit</a></b> for the <b>Critique Club</b>:<br/>I really like the composition. I''m happy that you chose to take this one outside rather than inside a studio. Gives it much more live. They people in the background add to the picture. People probably thought you were crazy lying in the ground with 4 rubber ducks taking pictures :) The only thing that I think could have been done better is the background. A simpler background. Maby white stone but keeping the people walking. A good picture all together. Good luck in future challanges.</td>', 'Critique by arnit for the Critique Club:I really like the composition. I''m happy that you chose to take this one outside rather than inside a studio. Gives it much more live. They people in the background add to the picture. People probably thought you were crazy lying in the ground with 4 rubber ducks taking pictures :) The only thing that I think could have been done better is the background. A simpler background. Maby white stone but keeping the people walking. A good picture all together. Good luck in future challanges.', '2006-05-10 23:16:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404480, 329309, 41802, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>Subject::<br/> <br/>"A Stitch in Time Saves Nine" was a clever idea for the Cliches and Sayings challenge.  This was a very creative idea.<br/> <br/>Technically::<br/> <br/>The image itself is a very nice shot.  I really do like the lighting, you have drawn direct attention to the subject we are supposed to be focusing on. You might have just stretched the lighting a little bit more so that the center spot was a little bit bigger.  The clarity and focus appear strong.  I would be curious to see the shot if you were able to make the stich line tight, at first glance I just thought it was a string before I read the title (during voting).  I can understand that it was probably pretty hard to set a tight string without having a hand in the photo which might cause more shadows.  You might even try something like the clear fishing wire, just a thought.  I also like your cropping and placement of the subject, we as voters know exactly what the subject was.  <br/> <br/>Summary:: <br/> <br/>Overall this was a nice entry and very creative.  I look forward to your future entries.</td>', '::Critique Club:: Subject:: "A Stitch in Time Saves Nine" was a clever idea for the Cliches and Sayings challenge.  This was a very creative idea. Technically:: The image itself is a very nice shot.  I really do like the lighting, you have drawn direct attention to the subject we are supposed to be focusing on. You might have just stretched the lighting a little bit more so that the center spot was a little bit bigger.  The clarity and focus appear strong.  I would be curious to see the shot if you were able to make the stich line tight, at first glance I just thought it was a string before I read the title (during voting).  I can understand that it was probably pretty hard to set a tight string without having a hand in the photo which might cause more shadows.  You might even try something like the clear fishing wire, just a thought.  I also like your cropping and placement of the subject, we as voters know exactly what the subject was.   Summary::  Overall this was a nice entry and very creative.  I look forward to your future entries.', '2006-05-11 00:50:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404489, 327995, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hello, Oddfrog from karmabreeze via CTP:M2!<br/> <br/>There are two very obvious downfalls to this photo. First being that the image is way too dark, and the second being that the foreground subjects aren''t crisply focused. It might be nice to see a little extra light splashed across the gifts, particularly the gold ribbon, which would then have a little sparkle. This would also take the couple further into the background. It also looks like there are some noise issues, which could be easily solved with a light run through Neat Image. (If you don''t have it, the demo version is free and since that version only works on photos up to 1024 pixels it works well for challenge entries that are limited to 640.)<br/> <br/>I do think, however, that for wedding photography this is a lovely idea. In terms of the challenge, the cliche isn''t half bad in matching the photo, which is more than I can say for a lot of higher scoring photos that only met the cliche halfway.</td>', 'Hello, Oddfrog from karmabreeze via CTP:M2! There are two very obvious downfalls to this photo. First being that the image is way too dark, and the second being that the foreground subjects aren''t crisply focused. It might be nice to see a little extra light splashed across the gifts, particularly the gold ribbon, which would then have a little sparkle. This would also take the couple further into the background. It also looks like there are some noise issues, which could be easily solved with a light run through Neat Image. (If you don''t have it, the demo version is free and since that version only works on photos up to 1024 pixels it works well for challenge entries that are limited to 640.) I do think, however, that for wedding photography this is a lovely idea. In terms of the challenge, the cliche isn''t half bad in matching the photo, which is more than I can say for a lot of higher scoring photos that only met the cliche halfway.', '2006-05-11 00:54:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404492, 327553, 28710, '<td valign="top">This is one of my favorite images in the challenge. Daring to enter something biblically themed. The 6.184 is a pretty fine score for something with such a controversial subject (sad though that may be).</td>', 'This is one of my favorite images in the challenge. Daring to enter something biblically themed. The 6.184 is a pretty fine score for something with such a controversial subject (sad though that may be).', '2006-05-11 00:55:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404521, 327988, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hi Margie!<br/> <br/>I''ve got a couple things on this photo -<br/> <br/>First, even though she''s your baby and always will be, she''s looking more like a toddler for the purposes of fitting into the "sleeping like a baby" cliche. It can be argued that "like" means she doesn''t have to be, but photos that need to have a case made for them rarely do well. So it may be that a lot of voters didn''t feel that the photo fully met its title - though there are a lot of high scoring photos that only met their titles halfway, so I was probably more strict on this issue than others. <br/> <br/>As to the quality of the photo, well, I think the light is wrong. It''s natural and I''m sure you didn''t want to wake her up, but there''s something cold and snapshottish about the blue tones. I would like to see this in a warmer, more golden tone. Also, the crop is too tight. Her head is cut off toward the top of the photo, and her hair at the right. So pull back a bit, warm up the light, and that will make a world of difference. :-)</td>', 'Hi Margie! I''ve got a couple things on this photo - First, even though she''s your baby and always will be, she''s looking more like a toddler for the purposes of fitting into the "sleeping like a baby" cliche. It can be argued that "like" means she doesn''t have to be, but photos that need to have a case made for them rarely do well. So it may be that a lot of voters didn''t feel that the photo fully met its title - though there are a lot of high scoring photos that only met their titles halfway, so I was probably more strict on this issue than others.  As to the quality of the photo, well, I think the light is wrong. It''s natural and I''m sure you didn''t want to wake her up, but there''s something cold and snapshottish about the blue tones. I would like to see this in a warmer, more golden tone. Also, the crop is too tight. Her head is cut off toward the top of the photo, and her hair at the right. So pull back a bit, warm up the light, and that will make a world of difference. :-)', '2006-05-11 01:06:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404546, 328045, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hi Alex -<br/> <br/>I actually love this concept for a cliche photo. Nice choice of subject matter both in the beautiful antique Poe and the Mickey Mouse inside. <br/> <br/>Critically speaking, the hands are blown out and blurred. Overall, I would like to see a clear picture throughout in this case. The title doesn''t need to be highlighted via DOF as it is now to get the point across. Even if the average viewer doesn''t read the cover title, the book itself looks academic and musty enough to convey your idea.</td>', 'Hi Alex - I actually love this concept for a cliche photo. Nice choice of subject matter both in the beautiful antique Poe and the Mickey Mouse inside.  Critically speaking, the hands are blown out and blurred. Overall, I would like to see a clear picture throughout in this case. The title doesn''t need to be highlighted via DOF as it is now to get the point across. Even if the average viewer doesn''t read the cover title, the book itself looks academic and musty enough to convey your idea.', '2006-05-11 01:15:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404549, 328163, 49202, '<td valign="top"><b>From the CTP MkII</b> <br/> <br/><b>First Impression:</b> Hah, fun! 7, ''cuz they look silly.;)<br/><b>Composition:</b> Subject placing''s fine. It''s the cropping I have a problem with. It''s a bit too thight, especially at the right of the photo. 5 or 6.<br/><b>Subject:</b> 8, because they''re silly and silly''s fun and I like fun so subject rocks.<br/><b>Technical:</b> I guess you went a bit too far toning down the colours, as the "daughter"''s garments lost their vibrancy. However, selectively desaturading the "mother"''s garments did good for your shot. So there. 6.<br/><b>Improvement:</b> A little wider crop, a bit more saturation on the daughter''s clothes, explosions on the background, and it''s a tenner.;p<br/><b>Summary:</b> Aye, it''s a fun photo. It''s what matters for me in the end.<br/> <br/><b>Disclaimer:</b> <i>The following crits are personal opinions, not photographic dogmas. Please see them as suggestions, not claims of mastery nor a show of hauteur.;p</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-11 06:23:09.</i></td>', 'From the CTP MkII  First Impression: Hah, fun! 7, ''cuz they look silly.;)Composition: Subject placing''s fine. It''s the cropping I have a problem with. It''s a bit too thight, especially at the right of the photo. 5 or 6.Subject: 8, because they''re silly and silly''s fun and I like fun so subject rocks.Technical: I guess you went a bit too far toning down the colours, as the "daughter"''s garments lost their vibrancy. However, selectively desaturading the "mother"''s garments did good for your shot. So there. 6.Improvement: A little wider crop, a bit more saturation on the daughter''s clothes, explosions on the background, and it''s a tenner.;pSummary: Aye, it''s a fun photo. It''s what matters for me in the end. Disclaimer: The following crits are personal opinions, not photographic dogmas. Please see them as suggestions, not claims of mastery nor a show of hauteur.;p', '2006-05-11 01:15:36.000000', '2006-05-11 07:23:09.000000', 0),
(2404558, 329309, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hi Christian -<br/> <br/>I scored this one pretty high, a 7. I think it suffered from being too dark for DPC tastes, and from the needle curving around the nine looking more like a scythe - I wouldn''t have recognized it as a needle, to be honest, and the shadow blends with it so well that it makes that identification that much more difficult.<br/> <br/>However, I definitely appreciate that this photo actually meets the challenge fully, as opposed to many high scoring images that only met it halfway.</td>', 'Hi Christian - I scored this one pretty high, a 7. I think it suffered from being too dark for DPC tastes, and from the needle curving around the nine looking more like a scythe - I wouldn''t have recognized it as a needle, to be honest, and the shadow blends with it so well that it makes that identification that much more difficult. However, I definitely appreciate that this photo actually meets the challenge fully, as opposed to many high scoring images that only met it halfway.', '2006-05-11 01:22:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404564, 328163, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hi Richard -<br/> <br/>After reading your notes, I absolutely agree with your decisions with regards to color desaturation - very effective, and quite lovely. The background could be better ideally, as you say, but I wouldn''t say that it truly distracts much from the women. Mom is a tiny bit out of focus, and I would have liked to see more clarity there. It was a good fit with the challenge, too. Nice work!</td>', 'Hi Richard - After reading your notes, I absolutely agree with your decisions with regards to color desaturation - very effective, and quite lovely. The background could be better ideally, as you say, but I wouldn''t say that it truly distracts much from the women. Mom is a tiny bit out of focus, and I would have liked to see more clarity there. It was a good fit with the challenge, too. Nice work!', '2006-05-11 01:25:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2404569, 328457, 10818, '<td valign="top">I think its a fantastic shot.  I would love to play with it, and make it just a tad darker.  Not much, just a bit.<br/> <br/>Awesome job, congrats man...its really a fine shot !</td>', 'I think its a fantastic shot.  I would love to play with it, and make it just a tad darker.  Not much, just a bit. Awesome job, congrats man...its really a fine shot !', '2006-05-11 01:28:24.000000', NULL, 0),
