(2405732, 327988, 24503, '<td valign="top">From the CTP MkII <br/> <br/>First Impression: it doesn''t deserves so low score, IMO. Cute girl.<br/> <br/>Composition: Maybe a bit too centered subject, needs some dynamism.<br/> <br/>Subject: Nice idea and good cliche. You''ve selected a wonderful girl, but maybe a little "old" to be considered a baby.<br/> <br/>Technical: I think the main problem with the score of this photo comes from the lightening. In interiors I think that is very difficult to lighten properly without the experience and equipment many DPCers have. I don''t know how to explain it but lights doesn''t look professional. And voters are very cruel with this... that''s DPC.<br/> <br/>Improvement: basically the light (see up^^).<br/> <br/>Summary: Nice idea and subject but needs a bit more work on lightening.<br/> <br/>Álex<br/></td>', 'From the CTP MkII  First Impression: it doesn''t deserves so low score, IMO. Cute girl. Composition: Maybe a bit too centered subject, needs some dynamism. Subject: Nice idea and good cliche. You''ve selected a wonderful girl, but maybe a little "old" to be considered a baby. Technical: I think the main problem with the score of this photo comes from the lightening. In interiors I think that is very difficult to lighten properly without the experience and equipment many DPCers have. I don''t know how to explain it but lights doesn''t look professional. And voters are very cruel with this... that''s DPC. Improvement: basically the light (see up^^). Summary: Nice idea and subject but needs a bit more work on lightening. Álex', '2006-05-11 12:10:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2405765, 327995, 24503, '<td valign="top">From the CTP MkII <br/> <br/>First Impression: A really nice idea and composition but a bit dark.<br/> <br/>Composition: I like composition, with both of you on the corner. Maybe it will improve if you put the names more in diagonal, not so frontal and create a guide line from left down to the present and you.<br/> <br/>Subject: OK, but if the present, the gift is the subject it should be more relevant in any way (maybe changing a bit the comosition as suggested).<br/> <br/>Technical: Here the image has the main flaw, IMO. The DOF is nice, maybe the focus should be more on the gift and less in the names, but the light is very poor here. You have a problem of light and you didn''t repair it in the postprocessing. I had the same problem in some of my first shots for DPC (and some of the late also, LOL). When you learn to PP more, your results improve a lot.<br/> <br/>Improvement: Basically light and white balance.<br/> <br/>Summary: Don''t even feel bad for the score, that''s a way of learning, maybe cruel (LOL), but I assure you will improve if follow shooting. Don''t stop making photos.<br/> <br/>Álex<br/></td>', 'From the CTP MkII  First Impression: A really nice idea and composition but a bit dark. Composition: I like composition, with both of you on the corner. Maybe it will improve if you put the names more in diagonal, not so frontal and create a guide line from left down to the present and you. Subject: OK, but if the present, the gift is the subject it should be more relevant in any way (maybe changing a bit the comosition as suggested). Technical: Here the image has the main flaw, IMO. The DOF is nice, maybe the focus should be more on the gift and less in the names, but the light is very poor here. You have a problem of light and you didn''t repair it in the postprocessing. I had the same problem in some of my first shots for DPC (and some of the late also, LOL). When you learn to PP more, your results improve a lot. Improvement: Basically light and white balance. Summary: Don''t even feel bad for the score, that''s a way of learning, maybe cruel (LOL), but I assure you will improve if follow shooting. Don''t stop making photos. Álex', '2006-05-11 12:25:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2405844, 329309, 24503, '<td valign="top">From the CTP MkII <br/> <br/>First Impression: wonderful idea, very good cliche selected.<br/> <br/>Composition: I like it, you use quite properly the rule of thirds.<br/> <br/>Subject: very nice clock. The thread is a bit too thick, IMO.<br/> <br/>Technical: I like you have nore light in the nine, but I don''t like the shadows, they are too intense for me. The upper side of the clock is a bit too black, without detail. The focus is good.<br/> <br/>Improvement: use a softer light. <br/> <br/>Summary: wonderful shot. Good job.<br/> <br/>Álex<br/></td>', 'From the CTP MkII  First Impression: wonderful idea, very good cliche selected. Composition: I like it, you use quite properly the rule of thirds. Subject: very nice clock. The thread is a bit too thick, IMO. Technical: I like you have nore light in the nine, but I don''t like the shadows, they are too intense for me. The upper side of the clock is a bit too black, without detail. The focus is good. Improvement: use a softer light.  Summary: wonderful shot. Good job. Álex', '2006-05-11 12:46:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2405910, 328163, 24503, '<td valign="top">From the CTP MkII <br/> <br/>First Impression: nice photo with a great concept.<br/> <br/>Composition: wonderful, with rhythm, using thirds, repetition,... really good.<br/> <br/>Subject: perfect. Very appopiate for the challenge.<br/> <br/>Technical: focus is tack sharp. You use DOF very well, assuming you want leave mother''s face a lit blurred. Colors of the daughter''s clothes works quite well. The clothes of the mother, on the other side, are too gray for me. <br/> <br/>Improvement: I think a bit more of saturation on mother''s clothes would have helped. As you say in your comments, the BG is a bit distracting. The other thing is quite personal, IMO it would have been better with the mother completely in focus, but it''s just an opinion.<br/> <br/>Summary: Wondeful shot that I think should have scored much better for me. But maybe I''m too generous compared to the average voter...LOL<br/> <br/>Álex<br/></td>', 'From the CTP MkII  First Impression: nice photo with a great concept. Composition: wonderful, with rhythm, using thirds, repetition,... really good. Subject: perfect. Very appopiate for the challenge. Technical: focus is tack sharp. You use DOF very well, assuming you want leave mother''s face a lit blurred. Colors of the daughter''s clothes works quite well. The clothes of the mother, on the other side, are too gray for me.  Improvement: I think a bit more of saturation on mother''s clothes would have helped. As you say in your comments, the BG is a bit distracting. The other thing is quite personal, IMO it would have been better with the mother completely in focus, but it''s just an opinion. Summary: Wondeful shot that I think should have scored much better for me. But maybe I''m too generous compared to the average voter...LOL Álex', '2006-05-11 13:01:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2405943, 327994, 24503, '<td valign="top">From the CTP MkII <br/> <br/>First Impression: Now I understand it, thanks. Nice shot.<br/> <br/>Composition: like the composition, as it is dynamic and creates a movement through the image.<br/> <br/>Subject: Nice subject, but a bit difficult to make a photo of, so it´s very shiny.<br/> <br/>Technical: Good use of DOF. The nerds are too brilliant, so the light is a bit harsh.<br/> <br/>Improvement: It''s a bit noisy, I don''t know if your ISO was too high.<br/> <br/>Summary: Good job.<br/> <br/>Álex<br/></td>', 'From the CTP MkII  First Impression: Now I understand it, thanks. Nice shot. Composition: like the composition, as it is dynamic and creates a movement through the image. Subject: Nice subject, but a bit difficult to make a photo of, so it´s very shiny. Technical: Good use of DOF. The nerds are too brilliant, so the light is a bit harsh. Improvement: It''s a bit noisy, I don''t know if your ISO was too high. Summary: Good job. Álex', '2006-05-11 13:08:18.000000', NULL, 0),
